WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.346 --> 00:00:08.197
Forms lets you build a form once, share it with a link or a QR code, and have the answers and documents arrive in your own storage.

2
00:00:08.900 --> 00:00:15.385
Open Forms in the sidebar. Each form shows its fields and its latest version. Open one to edit it.

3
00:00:16.085 --> 00:00:27.456
The palette on the left lists the field types. Choose one to add it after the selected field. Select any field to change its label, whether it is required, and its other properties on the right.

4
00:00:28.155 --> 00:00:33.488
Choose Save. Every save is a new version, and the Versions menu lets you look at an earlier one.

5
00:00:34.190 --> 00:00:38.585
Preview shows the form as a client sees it, on a desktop or on a phone.

6
00:00:41.243 --> 00:00:52.251
The Share tab holds the public address and its QR code. You changed the form after publishing it, so choose Publish changes to put the new version live. The address stays the same.

7
00:00:52.952 --> 00:00:58.904
This is what a client sees when they open the address. Their answers and files go straight to your storage.

8
00:00:59.606 --> 00:01:10.849
A personal link is made for one client. Enter a client or file reference, not a name, choose when it expires, and create it. You can copy it, show its QR code, or revoke it.

9
00:01:11.549 --> 00:01:18.802
Submissions lists what has arrived, with its status and where the files were saved. The answers themselves stay in your storage.

10
00:01:19.502 --> 00:01:24.579
That is Forms: build it, share it, and collect answers and documents in your own storage.
